## Original Content
Japan's fiscal 2027 budget requests are expected to top 130 trillion yen (about $818 billion), driven largely by a record defense expenditure request of around 8.9 trillion yen, Kyodo News reported on Friday.

## Summary
Japan's fiscal 2027 budget requests are expected to surpass 130 trillion yen (about $818 billion), primarily due to a record defense expenditure of around 8.9 trillion yen. This significant increase in defense spending is placing pressure on the overall budget. Kyodo News reported this development.

## Key Points
- Japan's fiscal 2027 budget is projected to exceed 130 trillion yen, equivalent to approximately $818 billion.
- A record defense spending request of around 8.9 trillion yen is the main driver of the budget increase.
- The defense expenditure represents a historic high, as indicated by Kyodo News.
- This surge in defense spending is creating financial strain for the government's budget.


